<%# locals: (venture: nil) %>
<%# Fuime: the only lesson that is about Fuime, kept deliberately short.

    Every figure is read from the object that owns it. A learn page with "5%"
    typed into it becomes a page that lies the first time pricing changes, and it
    is the one page a founder would be entitled to be angry about. %>

<p>
  This is the short one, because it is the only part of the whole reading list
  that is about us rather than about running a business.
</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-2 mb-0">The fee</h2>

<p>
  Fuime keeps
  <strong><%= Fuime::PaymentLinkService::FUIME_PLATFORM_FEE_PERCENT %>%</strong>
  of what a customer pays. That is the standard rate. A school programme or a
  waived venture can be lower, and the figure for your own business is shown on
  your storefront and on every sale in your ledger.
</p>

<% if Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
  <p>
    There is a floor of
    <strong><%= number_to_currency(Event::Plan::MINIMUM_FEE_CENTS / 100.0) %></strong>
    per sale, because processing a card costs a fixed amount however small the
    payment is. Worth knowing before you build a business on it: the smaller your
    typical sale, the bigger a share of it the fee is. Selling one thing at a
    larger price and selling ten things at a tenth of it are not the same
    business.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-2 mb-0">Where the money is until you are paid</h2>

<% if Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
  <p>
    When somebody buys from your storefront they are buying from Fuime LLC, and
    your business fulfils the order. That is why their receipt and their card
    statement say Fuime, and it is why we handle a refund if they want one.
    Expect to be asked about it. "Who is Fuime on my statement?" is a normal
    question, and the answer is that they are the payment side of your business.
  </p>
  <p>
    What that leaves you is money Fuime owes you and settles later. It is not a
    balance sitting in an account of yours. Fuime is not a bank and does not hold
    deposits. Your ledger shows what has been earned and what has been paid out,
    and the difference is what you are owed.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p>
    The money goes into a Stripe account your parent or guardian owns, in your
    business's name, and Fuime never holds it. That structure is the reason
    somebody under 18 can take card payments at all: the account belongs to an
    adult who can legally sign for it, and you operate it.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-2 mb-0">Getting it out</h2>

<p>
  Money leaving your business goes through a payout, and a payout needs your
  guardian to approve it. They are the adult who signs for your business, and
  money leaving it is exactly the thing they signed for.
</p>

<% unless StripeService.live? %>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Right now Fuime runs against Stripe's test mode. Payment pages work from end
    to end so you can see all of this happen, but no real money moves and no real
    card is charged. We will say so plainly, here and in the product, before that
    changes.
  </p>
<% end %>

<div class="card">
  <p class="m-0 text-sm">
    Work your own version out once: take a price you are thinking of charging,
    subtract the fee above, then subtract what the job costs you. What is left is
    what the job actually pays. If that number surprises you, the fix is almost
    never selling more of them.
    <%= link_to "The numbers lesson", learn_lesson_path(slug: "the-numbers", venture: venture&.slug), class: "underline" %>
    covers why.
  </p>
</div>
